{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b> unto the altar that is before YHWH.</b> This is the golden altar, which is before YHWH — in the Heikhal. And what does וְיָצָא teach? Because he performed the sprinklings upon the parokhet and stood from the altar and inward and sprinkled, and in the gifts of the altar it required him to go out from the altar and to the outside, and begin from the corner on the northeast (Yoma 58)." "<b>And he shall make atonement upon it.</b> What is its atonement? <b>And he shall take of the blood of the bull and of the blood of the goat</b> — mixed one into the other (ibid. 57)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:47.017634329Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}